Þríauga — third-party data and attribution
==========================================

The application source in this repository is covered by LICENSE.

The generated dictionary and media packs, published as release assets, are
derived from the sources below. They are redistributed under CC BY-SA 4.0 to
satisfy the share-alike terms of the sources that require it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
CC-CEDICT — Chinese–English dictionary
  124,880 entries
  https://www.mdbg.net/chinese/dictionary?page=cc-cedict
  Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0

Folkets lexikon — Swedish–English dictionary
  95,443 entries, plus 30,807 example sentences and idioms
  Kungliga Tekniska högskolan (KTH) / Språkbanken
  https://folkets-lexikon.csc.kth.se/
  Licence: CC BY-SA 2.5 Generic

Wiktionary — etymologies, inflected forms, sense examples, pronunciation
  1,629,915 entries · 550,378 etymologies · 1,144,654 inflected forms
  Extracted with wiktextract, via https://kaikki.org
  https://en.wiktionary.org
  Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0 and GFDL

Tatoeba — example sentences
  118,692 aligned sentence pairs (English–Swedish, English–Chinese)
  https://tatoeba.org
  Licence: CC BY 2.0 FR

Wikimedia Commons — illustrations and pronunciation audio
  5,715 images · 30,738 audio recordings
  https://commons.wikimedia.org
  Licences: per file (CC0, Public Domain, CC BY, CC BY-SA, GFDL)
  Each image and audio clip stores its own licence and author, and the
  application displays them alongside the media.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Only freely-licensed media is included. Files hosted locally on Wikipedia
rather than Commons — typically non-free — are excluded by the build.

Chinese–Swedish word pairs are derived through English, because no free
direct Chinese–Swedish lexicon exists. The application labels such results.
